            <ArticleTitle>Supraclavicular Brachial Plexus Block for Arteriovenous Hemodialysis Access Procedures.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>749-52</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jvir.2016.02.003</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1051-0443(16)00231-1</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ultrasound-guided supraclavicular brachial plexus block using 1% and 2% lidocaine in 21 procedures is reported. Average procedure time was 5.1 minutes (± 1.2 min; range, 2-8 min). Average time of onset and duration were 4.8 minutes (± 3.7 min; range, 0-10 min) and 77.9 minutes (± 26.7 min; range, 44-133 min), respectively, for sensory block and 8.4 minutes (± 5.7 min; range, 3-23 min) and 99 minutes (± 40.5 min; range, 45-171 min), respectively, for motor block. The pain scale assessment averaged 0.4 (± 1.1; range, 0-4). There were no complications.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Copyright © 2016 SIR. Published by Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
